.SH BUGS
.I Chess
reads only a file's first game.
Null moves and Chess960 are not taken.
.br
Weiss searches on its one thread, as APE has one,
and looks at its input every 2048 positions for
.BR stop ,
by the bytes waiting in a pipe:
from a terminal it does not see
.B stop
until it has searched,
and when its input ends while it searches with no limit, it goes on.
.br
Acme's guard on a window's writes is one for the window, which the next open of its body takes:
another program that sets it at the same moment, as
.IR hl (1)
does as it colors, can make a write of
.I Chess
fail, or one of its own.
A write longer than 4096 bytes goes in pieces, one
.BR Undo ;
an edit by another program between two pieces leaves part of the rewrite.
